      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9b565e4ad7346113",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did āśīrvād mean, and what did praṇām mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: फूल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फूल (phūl) — \"a flower\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit phulla, 'blossomed, opened out', from phull-, 'to bloom'. So the Hindi word for a flower is at bottom a word for the act of opening, with the object named after the event."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The double ll collapsed and paid for itself by lengthening the vowel in front of it, which is the standard trade in this family — the same bargain that gave you कान out of karṇa. It is also the measure of lightness: something that weighs nothing at all is phūl jaisā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things at a welcome."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "phūl",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *phūl*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "phūl, then praṇām, the flower and the bow at the door",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *phūl*, then *praṇām*, the flower and the bow at the door]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
