          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मेज़",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मेज़ (mez) — \"a table\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian mez, and behind the Persian sits Portuguese mesa, out of Latin mēnsa. Portuguese ships carried the object and its name into the Indian Ocean, which is the same route that brought कमरा in from camera."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There was no inherited word for a raised surface on four legs because the household had not had one; people ate and wrote and worked at floor level. The word arrived with the furniture, which is usually how that happens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and one of them came off a ship."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
